  "implementation": "In the opted-in GPU test process, an idle, initialized OCR reader can prepare detector boxes for one pending capture during the original 120 ms selection window. The worker owns the captured copy and a separate detector preprocessing instance; native sessions keep per-thread requests. One task at a time. Actual reads still use the buffer-selected generation and sequence. Only a ready result with the same provider, dtype, geometry and exact detector input pixels can supply boxes. Recognition, page qualification and publication remain on the selected-frame path. CPU default launch, cold first frame and busy sampling retain their prior scheduling.",
